          "name": "How fast should my WordPress website load?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most performance experts recommend a load time under 2.5 seconds for the Largest Contentful Paint (LCP). Anything above 4 seconds is generally considered slow and likely to hurt both rankings and conversions."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the single most effective way to speed up a WordPress site?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Upgrading to quality, WordPress-optimized hosting usually produces the biggest single improvement, since it strengthens the foundation everything else depends on. Caching and image optimization come close behind as high-impact fixes."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I need a premium caching plugin, or is a free one enough?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Free plugins like WP Super Cache or LiteSpeed Cache work well for most standard sites. Premium options like WP Rocket are worth considering if you want automated settings and built-in extras like lazy loading and database cleanup."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Will optimizing my images hurt their visual quality?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Modern compression tools reduce file size while keeping visual quality nearly identical to the original, often shrinking files by 60 to 80 percent without noticeable loss."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does switching my WordPress theme really make a noticeable difference?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Heavy, feature-loaded themes load significantly more CSS and JavaScript. Switching to a fast theme like GeneratePress or Astra often produces an immediate, measurable improvement in load time."
          }
